Falsifies `domain_name_system::proofs::the_dotted_parse_accepts_exactly_names`.

The defect: the dotted parse no longer refuses an empty label, so `a..b` is taken as a name with a
zero length byte inside it, which ends the name early on the wire.

Expected to fail: `assert!(is_name, ...)` on `Ok`, for a text with two dots together or a dot at
its start.

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -279,9 +279,6 @@
                     end += 1;
                 }
                 let label = &body[start..end];
-                if label.is_empty() {
-                    return Err(Error::BadLabel);
-                }
                 if label.len() > MAXIMUM_LABEL_BYTES {
                     return Err(Error::LabelTooLong);
                 }
